9o6|n|A thin film of liquid inflated with air or gas; as, a soap bubble; bubbles on the surface of a river. ; A small quantity of air or gas within a liquid body; as, bubbles rising in champagne or aerated waters. ; A globule of air, or globular vacuum, in a transparent solid; as, bubbles in window glass, or in a lens. ; A small, hollow, floating bead or globe, formerly used for testing the strength of spirits. ; The globule of air in the spirit tube of a level. ; Anything that wants firmness or solidity; that which is more specious than real; a false show; a cheat or fraud; a delusive scheme; an empty project; a dishonest speculation; as, the South Sea bubble. ; A person deceived by an empty project; a gull. ; To rise in bubbles, as liquids when boiling or agitated; to contain bubbles. ; To run with a gurgling noise, as if forming bubbles; as, a bubbling stream. ; To sing with a gurgling or warbling sound.	n:1vb,58,4~1vb,58,4
